    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d22">

                <pb facs="0084" n="14" sameAs="frus:frus1919Parisv01/pg14"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Inquiry files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Walter Lippmann to the Secretary of War</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Baker</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">New York</hi>
                        </placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-05">November 5,
                            1917</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dear N. D. B.</hi>: Your suggestion is ideal. I had
                    not dared to hope that General Bliss would be able to give any time to the
                    matter, and had had it in mind that General Crowder would be the best of all the
                    men that I had known in the Department for this particular subject.</p>
                <p>I rather expect to go to Washington next week, with the chief inducement the hope
                    of seeing you.</p>
                <p>Ever yours,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walter Lippmann</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
